{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>An altar of earth you shall make for Me.</b> Ibn Ezra explained (on Exodus 20:21) that He said <b>You shall not make with Me gods of silver and gods of gold</b> — to draw supernal power into their forms, so that they would be intermediaries between Me and you. But <b>in every place where I cause My name to be mentioned I will come to you</b> — I, in My glory — <b>and I will bless you</b>; you have no need for an intermediary at all. And according to the opinion of our Sages (Mekhilta, here), it is concerning the altars — those made in the Tabernacle and in the Temple — that He mentioned the commandment of altars of earth and of stones, to say that they shall make the altars for HaShem alone, and there they shall sacrifice burnt-offerings and peace-offerings, and not to the shedim in the open field; and in every place where they mention His name, He will come in His glory upon them, to cause His Shekhinah to dwell among them and to bless them."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:12:05.019005432Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}